 longer initializing a `base::Clock` in this class?"]],0,62],[7112562,20398,187,4.21,3.407,[[0,1.0,51,189]],[["049a82a5_8a600855",50,-2,1,"Wrap this in `ASSIGN_OR_RETURN(...)`"],["808e2a29_2d57b23e",51,-2,1,"You still need to remove dev mode apps (as these two cannot co-exist)."],["847ff00e_f0fc25ec",50,-2,0,"Nit: this two lines can be merged and then maybe_app can be just app - it is guaranted in the scope it is correct (go/totw/165)"],["fd7ac086_c983c397",51,-2,0,"This was only a protector against uninstalling _unmanaged_ apps when they are not in the _managed_ allowlist. You can remove this check, as managed allowlist is also checked during AppActionInstall…"]],0,63],[7156529,20424,56,1.341,1.058,[[0,0.97,52,55],[12,0.03,1,1]],[["09fa5a70_8fff94de",52,-8,1,"I'd trust the renderer here and do a CHECK for non-emptiness."],["408874b0_c7041b08",53,-8,1,"Let's just have a public member like the rest of the fields? And perhaps shorten it to iwa_update_manifest_url."],["47e61504_77ddd526",54,-8,0,"Why isn't this a part of options.iwa_options?"],["561bf23c_868f031b",53,-8,1,"nit: mention that this has a lesser precedence than the policy setting"],["60d5ca85_7356fe9f",54,-8,1,"You fell into a trap! L529 will overwrite the update_manifest_url with the one stored in `isolation_data` 😊 (might make sense to add a test for this!)"],["6eef5750_7a426277",55,-8,1,"Let's do a proper GURL here and below"],["dd37af02_88a5d6eb",56,-8,1,"nitty nit: since this func is already talking about isolation data lala, let's just use `update_manifest_url` here for brevity. (or `iwa_update_manifest_url`)"],["f2a6c061_77d8af1f",52,-8,1,"On a side note... why are we doing this here and not in the ManifestToWebAppInstallInfoJob?"]],0,64],[7161815,20424,415,7.601,6.192,[[0,53]],[["246a4060_2b0632ec",57,-11,1,"It is no longer true after your CL"],["56361dff_57ea223f",58,-8,1,"Can we do a simple `result[url_info->web_bundle_id()] = ...`?"],["5a4f1cd4_f79cf0f6",58,-8,0,"Do a CHECK() here."],["78275f05_3973cf2b",58,-8,1,"ditto here"],["7f4862cc_12d1610e",58,-8,1,"This can't be true (it's not a valid GURL then)."],["b934ea2c_f5254005",58,-8,1,"nit: you don't need to set these two -- you already have defaults."],["ca958dc5_ced682c9",59,-8,1,"This just looks like the normal manifest. Why do we need to mock it? I'm a bit concerned that we're adding too many various methods to the test server despite it being a simple container for correct…"],["4056f6a0_1d944764",54,-5,1,"Is this really worth it? I'm mainly assuming that * The chance of an org admin suddenly deciding to uninstall an IWA is insanely low (as this is normally something contractual) -- ask Mirco 😊 * The…"],["e11b0866_b0972531",58,-5,1,"Maybe ``` GetIsolatedWebAppsWithOnlyUserManagement() ``` ?"],["7fe28a78_e9432f0e",50,-4,1,"Please keep FinalizeInstall here and add a next step callback to ProcessInstallInfoResultAndProceed"],["8c04a355_7b77348e",50,-4,1,"This doesn't look good unless I'm missing something obvious. `expected_version` will only be set if the policy explicitly lists it; this won't help with installing a managed v2.0 without version…"],["dd7aea9f_ce2dce67",50,-4,1,"This looks scary! Let's rewrite it."],["0eaf9755_64b47c88",57,-1,1,"It seems that your change also allows for this one-app update type for user installed apps, am I right?"],["2bebb0af_2f82de08",60,-1,1,"This is not defined/used."],["3259a46c_f36e3c3a",58,-1,0,"@greengrape@google.com, Can we rely here (and in other Updater methods) on unsafe registrar, while for PolicyManager we lock it, for checking if apps are installed. Could you help me better…"],["495d40da_920a479a",50,-1,0,"Is it possible that it has no value? How/why it may happen that the installed version is lower than the one in the isolation data? Why we remove the browsing data in those cases? Could you clarify…"],["681fc0b0_98bb0a42",50,-1,1,"Does this cause an UAF since we already `std::move` the `install_info` as part of the `FinalizeInstall()`'s 2nd parameter, or is this somehow safe because the order of evaluation in C++ is not…"],["b37fc8dc_30b6c0ce",58,-1,0,"Once Andrew's CL about adding support for `WebAppFilter` to the `WebAppRegistrar` goes in [1], I believe we can add a new `WebAppFilter` (something similar to [2]) that only returns the IWAs which…"]],0,65],[7204390,20425,151,4.21,3.407,[[0,54]],[["01b4fed7_d39d2a70",36,-2,1,"This can be moved into the if block"],["1a59c77b_00148b03",36,-2,1,"Do a switch here!"],["2fcd5d5f_ac0047a8",36,-2,1,"Not needed?"],["34fd258e_94c1a08f",36,-2,1,"You can move this directly to L1202?"],["b1e2873f_0b046318",36,-2,1,"Something like ``` auto available_secondary_types = {type1, type2}; std::erase(available_secondary_types, primary_key_type); ``` Would be much simpler"],["db05526c_cc21fd89",36,-2,1,"This is a block for `!is_iwa`. What's the point of generating a `web_bundle_id` here?"],["fe30825c_962f9869",36,-2,1,"Can't we reuse this function somehow? IIUC there's a lot of duplication happening right now."],["f8e2d08a_2b8b209c",36,-1,1,"```suggestion NOTREACHED() << \"Unknown SignedWebBundleId::Type encountered.\"; ```"]],0,66],[7231609,20434,746,10.971,8.929,[[0,0.944,55,716],[1,0.033,4,24],[3,0.018,4,7],[5,0.005,21,3]],[["0167c25b_fe972e6d",33,-2,1,"Interesing! Have a product-y question. Let's say an IWA pop-up was launched which triggered a window.open() notification. After that, other things happened which triggered more notifications…"],["10361c7a_8523f758",23,-2,1,"AI SLOP!!! AI SLOP!!!"],["2cae4d86_8ccfca15",23,-2,1,"Why?"],["471698ab_1cdc966c",61,-2,0,"Possibly for a future re-write if it makes sense, maybe the opening of app settings can be hooked up via the `SettingsClick()` [1] function instead of `Click()`? That way, we don't have to worry…"],["8236bb70_4991084f",23,-2,1,"Can you actually keep a `provider_` raw ref in the class itself? There are way too many calls to `web_app::WebAppProvider::GetForWebApps(profile())` around."],["86656bbe_b1b3d341",0,-2,1,"what is it doing instead?"],["c0159466_0c533305",33,-2,1,"nit: Consolidate into a single getter (here and in other tests)? ``` std::optional<message_center::Notification> notification = display_service_tester_->GetNotification(notification_id);…"],["cd3a9ef1_158567d6",23,-2,1,"revert"],["cf8ec629_be9d028f",61,-2,1,"nit: `if (button_index == kSettingsButtonIndex)`, optional takes care of null checking"],["e5215bc7_79f582f9",23,-2,1,"We're now fancy and can use `lock.registrar().GetApps(WebAppFilter::IsIsolated())`"],["61058997_fe800e26",23,-1,0,"Aaaah is this to \"resurface\" the notification to the top of the list of active notifications? Nice! I wonder if there is a way to update the notification, like…"]],0,67],[7233150,20434,369,7.601,6.192,[[0,0.984,56,2206],[5,0.007,22,13],[2,0.006,8,12],[4,0.002,4,4],[6,0.001,4,2]],[["3b0dc93b_0eea0b4c",62,-2,1,"Is this changed needed for this rename, or was this a remnant of the parent CL or perhaps the next CL?"]],0,68],[7255917,20434,750,10.971,8.929,[[0,0.944,57,720],[1,0.032,5,24],[3,0.018,5,7],[5,0.005,23,3]],[],0,69],[7260736,20438,369,7.601,6.192,[[0,0.984,58,2218],[5,0.007,24,13],[2,0.006,9,12],[4,0.002,5,4],[6,0.001,5,2]],[],0,70],[7241670,20438,28,0.737,0.556,[[0,59]],[["24703fe8_c0bc0823",63,-5,1,"nit: this doesn't have to be a unique_ptr."]],0,71],[7265246,20439,9,0.421,0.3,[[5,25]],[],0,72],[7269272,20440,4,0.164,0.113,[[1,0.5,6,2],[3,0.5,6,2]],[],0,73]]}